    <task id="LOCAL-00184" summary="--  implemented the file type penalty system for the context search! Here's what was added:&#10;   &#10;     1. Configuration Model (ContextConfig.kt:171-245)&#10;   &#10;     Added three new penalty/boost maps to BoostConfig:&#10;     - fileTypePenalties: Penalize specific file extensions (e.g., pdf=0.5, md=0.7)&#10;     - filePatternPenalties: Penalize files matching glob patterns (e.g., **/docs/**=0.6)&#10;     - chunkKindBoosts: Boost/penalize based on chunk type (e.g., CODE_CLASS=1.3, PARAGRAPH=0.7)&#10;   &#10;     2. Penalty Application Logic (HybridContextProvider.kt:138-236)&#10;   &#10;     Implemented penalty calculation that:&#10;     - Applies file type penalties based on extension&#10;     - Matches glob patterns for path-based penalties (supports ** and * wildcards)&#10;     - Applies chunk kind boosts/penalties&#10;     - Combines all penalties multiplicatively (e.g., 0.5 × 0.6 × 0.7 = 0.21)&#10;     - Preserves original scores in metadata for transparency&#10;     - Re-ranks results after applying penalties to ensure doc files are pushed down&#10;   &#10;     3. Default Configuration (fusionagent.toml:338-383)&#10;   &#10;     Added comprehensive default penalties:&#10;     - PDFs, DOC/DOCX: 50% penalty (heavily penalized)&#10;     - Markdown, TXT: 30% penalty (lightly penalized)&#10;     - Docs directories: 40% penalty&#10;     - Code chunks (CLASS, FUNCTION, METHOD): 30% boost&#10;     - Documentation chunks (PARAGRAPH, DOCSTRING): 30% penalty&#10;   &#10;     4. Comprehensive Tests (HybridContextProviderTest.kt:345-605)&#10;   &#10;     Added 8 new tests verifying:&#10;     - File type penalties work correctly&#10;     - Glob pattern matching works (e.g., **/docs/** matches project/docs/guide.md)&#10;     - Chunk kind boosts work correctly&#10;     - Penalties combine multiplicatively&#10;     - Metadata preservation&#10;     - Ranking order is affected by penalties&#10;     - Empty config works (no penalties applied)&#10;   &#10;     Key Design Decisions&#10;   &#10;     1. When penalties are applied:&#10;     - Penalties are applied AFTER RRF (Reciprocal Rank Fusion) aggregation&#10;     - Results are then re-sorted by penalized scores&#10;     - This ensures penalties affect both scores AND rankings&#10;   &#10;     2. Score preservation:&#10;     - Original scores are preserved in original_score metadata&#10;     - Penalty multipliers are visible in metadata (file_type_penalty, pattern_penalty, kind_boost, combined_multiplier)&#10;     - Provides full transparency for debugging&#10;   &#10;     3. Glob matching:&#10;     - Supports ** (match anything including /)&#10;     - Supports * (match anything except /)&#10;     - Pattern **/README* correctly matches both README.md and docs/README.md --">
