    <task id="LOCAL-00192" summary="-- Changes Made&#10;   &#10;     1. QueryContextTool.kt (src/main/kotlin/com/orchestrator/mcp/tools/QueryContextTool.kt:27-47)&#10;   &#10;     Before:&#10;     - &quot;Use short, specific keywords (like grep/find commands)&quot;&#10;     - &quot;2-5 words&quot;&#10;   &#10;     After:&#10;     - &quot;Use domain-specific descriptive phrases (5-10 words) with concrete terms&quot;&#10;     - Mentions the semantic model (sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2)&#10;     - Better examples showing descriptive queries&#10;   &#10;     2. McpServerImpl.kt (src/main/kotlin/com/orchestrator/mcp/McpServerImpl.kt:2364+)&#10;   &#10;     Updated sections:&#10;   &#10;     1. Main CRITICAL guidance (line 2368):&#10;       - Changed from: &quot;Use SHORT keywords (2-5 words)&quot;&#10;       - Changed to: &quot;Use domain-specific descriptive phrases (5-10 words) with concrete technical terms&quot;&#10;       - Added explanation about semantic model understanding meaning&#10;     2. Good Query Examples (line 2420):&#10;       - Extended all examples from 3-4 words to 5-8 words&#10;       - Example: &quot;authentication JWT token&quot; → &quot;authentication JWT token validation implementation&quot;&#10;     3. Query Formulation Section (line 2448):&#10;       - New formula emphasizing domain terms + technical concepts + implementation details&#10;       - Explicitly mentions optimal length: 5-10 words&#10;       - Notes that semantic model understands meaning and context&#10;     4. Comparison Table (line 2465):&#10;       - All &quot;Good Query&quot; examples now use 5-8 word descriptive phrases&#10;       - Example: &quot;TaskRepository class&quot; → &quot;TaskRepository database access implementation&quot;&#10;     5. User Phrase Mapping (line 2408):&#10;       - Updated all suggested queries to be more descriptive&#10;       - Example: &quot;feature implementation&quot; → &quot;feature implementation core logic flow&quot;&#10;   &#10;     Rationale&#10;   &#10;     The changes reflect that:&#10;     - Semantic search with sentence-transformers benefits from richer context, not just keywords&#10;     - Domain-specific vocabulary provides better signals than generic grep-like terms&#10;     - 5-10 words is optimal for semantic understanding while staying focused&#10;     - Question words and abstract meta-queries still fail (kept those warnings)&#10;     - Concrete technical terms work better than vague concepts&#10;   &#10;     The tool will now guide users to write queries like:&#10;     - ✅ &quot;PGP encryption FTP adapter file transfer configuration&quot;&#10;     - ✅ &quot;consensus workflow voting mechanism implementation&quot;&#10;   &#10;     Instead of:&#10;     - ❌ &quot;PGP encryption&quot; (too short, lacks context)&#10;     - ❌ &quot;how does PGP encryption work in FTP?&quot; (question format)&#10;   &#10;     This better leverages the semantic search capabilities while still avoiding natural language questions that fail! --">
